=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# ssh screen-not-read ------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Mock: SSH Login. web-01.example.net runs Ubuntu 26.04 (OpenSSH$
# 10.2p1, ssh.socket). ubuntu2604 before its first connection:$
# no /run/sshd, so sshd -T fails.$
$
# SSH Login ####################################################$
$
  [?] SSH Login            Unknown can't read$
                           - Counted as not configured$
  [?] SSH Auth             Unknown can't read$
                           - Counted as not configured$
  [?] SSH Port             Unknown can't read$
                           - Counted as not configured$
$
# SSH Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
  [?] Root SSH Login       Can't read$
  [?] Password Login       Can't read$
  [?] SSH Port             Can't read$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disallow root login  Root can't log in over SSH$
   2) Key-only login       Turn password login off$
   3) Change SSH port      Now not read$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-3 or q]:$
$
$

